#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:4
msgid "Debugging the firmware"
msgstr "调试固件"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:6
msgid ""
"On-hardware debugging means halting the processor, setting breakpoints in "
"the C source, single-stepping, and inspecting variables, memory, registers, "
"and peripherals -- from inside VS Code. This needs three things: a **debug "
"build**, a **SWD debug probe** (a Segger J-Link), and the **Cortex-Debug** "
"extension driving ``arm-none-eabi-gdb`` against a J-Link GDB server."
msgstr ""
"硬件调试是指在 VS Code 内部暂停处理器、在 C 源码中设置断点、单步执行，并检查变量、内存、寄存器和外设。这需要三样东西：一个 "
"**调试构建**\\ 、一个 **SWD 调试探头**\\ （Segger J-Link），以及驱动 ``arm-none-eabi-gdb`` 连接 "
"J-Link GDB 服务器的 **Cortex-Debug** 扩展。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:14
msgid "Build for debugging"
msgstr "构建调试版本"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:16
msgid "Always rebuild the target with ``DEBUG=1``::"
msgstr "始终使用 ``DEBUG=1`` 重新构建目标：："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:20
msgid ""
"A release (``DEBUG=0``) image is compiled ``-O2``; in the debugger you will "
"see ``<optimized out>`` for many variables, inlined functions collapse into "
"their callers, and stepping jumps around unpredictably. ``DEBUG=1`` builds "
"``-Og -ggdb3``, which is debuggable while still booting on the camera. The "
"ELF you point the debugger at is::"
msgstr ""
"发布版（\\ ``DEBUG=0``\\ ）镜像以 ``-O2`` 编译；在调试器中你会看到许多变量显示为 ``<optimized out>``\\ "
"，内联函数会折叠进它们的调用者中，单步执行会不可预测地来回跳转。\\ ``DEBUG=1`` 以 ``-Og -ggdb3`` "
"构建，既可调试又仍能在摄像头上启动。你让调试器指向的 ELF 文件是：："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:28
msgid ""
"(For the Alif AE3, debug ``build/OPENMV_AE3/bin/firmware_M55_HP.elf`` -- the"
" high-performance core.)"
msgstr ""
"（对于 Alif AE3，调试 ``build/OPENMV_AE3/bin/firmware_M55_HP.elf`` —— 即高性能核心。）"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:32
msgid "The hardware: J-Link over SWD"
msgstr "硬件：通过 SWD 连接的 J-Link"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:34
msgid ""
"Connect a Segger J-Link to the camera's **SWD** pins (SWDIO, SWCLK, GND, and"
" target VCC for reference; the camera is powered over USB as usual). A "
"J-Link EDU / Base / Pro all work. Where the debug pins surface differs per "
"camera -- many boards have a dedicated JTAG/SWD connector, others expose SWD"
" on the I/O header or on test pads -- so check that board's pinout diagram "
"and schematic in the OpenMV hardware documentation for which pins to wire. "
"Install the **J-Link Software and Documentation Pack** from `segger.com "
"<https://www.segger.com/downloads/jlink/>`__ on the machine the probe is "
"physically plugged into. Keep it reasonably current -- older J-Link software"
" will not know the newer device names (STM32N6, MIMXRT, Alif)."
msgstr ""
"将 Segger J-Link 连接到摄像头的 **SWD** 引脚（SWDIO、SWCLK、GND，以及作为参考的目标 VCC；摄像头照常通过 USB"
" 供电）。J-Link EDU / Base / Pro 均可使用。调试引脚的引出位置因摄像头而异 —— 许多板子有专用的 JTAG/SWD "
"连接器，另一些则在 I/O 排针或测试焊盘上引出 SWD —— 因此请查阅 OpenMV "
"硬件文档中该板子的引脚图和原理图，以确定要接哪些引脚。在物理连接探头的那台机器上，从 `segger.com "
"<https://www.segger.com/downloads/jlink/>`__ 安装 **J-Link Software and "
"Documentation Pack**\\ 。请保持其版本相对较新 —— 较旧的 J-Link "
"软件不会识别较新的设备名称（STM32N6、MIMXRT、Alif）。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/production/firmware/debugging.rst:46
msgid ""
"Each MCU needs its exact J-Link **device name** so the probe loads the right"
" flash loader and memory map:"
msgstr "每个 MCU 都需要其确切的 J-Link **设备名称**\\ ，以便探头加载正确的闪存加载器和内存映射："

